---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Contribute"
  description="How to contribute to PHPRise: prerequisites, the flow, the rules and the code of conduct."
  path="/contribute"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contribute</p>
      <h1>No permission required</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Every repository accepts contributions under the same rules. Read them once and
        they apply everywhere.
      </p>

      <div class="prose mt-2">
        <h2>Before you start</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>PHP 8.4 or newer, with Composer.</li>
          <li>An issue describing what you intend to change, or an existing one to claim.</li>
          <li>Agreement with the <a href="/manifesto">manifesto</a> — it is a constraint, not a suggestion.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The flow</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Fork the repository and create a branch from the default branch.</li>
          <li>Write the failing test first, then the smallest change that makes it pass.</li>
          <li>Run the test suite and the static analysis configured in the repository.</li>
          <li>Open a pull request that explains the why, not only the what.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>The rules that are not negotiable</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>One level of indentation per method.</li>
          <li>No <code>else</code>.</li>
          <li>Primitives wrapped in value objects.</li>
          <li>Collections as first class objects.</li>
          <li>One dot per line.</li>
          <li>No abbreviations.</li>
          <li>Small entities: 50 lines per class, 10 files per package.</li>
          <li>At most two instance variables per class.</li>
          <li>No getters, setters or public properties.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Where your change belongs</h2>
        <p>
          If you are adding generic behaviour, it belongs in an atom. If you are wiring
          atoms together, it belongs in an assembly. Only business rules belong in an
          application. A pull request that puts framework code inside a domain layer will
          be rejected regardless of the tests.
        </p>

        <h2>Code of conduct</h2>
        <p>
          Be precise, be generous, attack the code and never the person. The full text is
          in the
          <a href="https://github.com/phprise-foundation/template/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md" rel="noopener">code of conduct</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__actions">
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/phprise-foundation" rel="noopener">Find a repository ↗</a>
        <a class="button button--ghost" href="/projects">Browse projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
